One of the distinguishing features of contextual definition, is that it does not
involve saying what the meaning of the phrase being defined is. Instead a systematic way of
constructing alternative sentences that exemplify its meaning is provided.
In Wittgenstein's hands this became the basis of an entire philosophy of
language.


